		"49-key keyboard",
		"PERFORMANCE: Master level, Pitch stick, Mod wheel",
		"SLOTS / PROGRAM: Slot A, Slot B, Slot C, Slot D, Display, Program dial",
		"SYNTH ENGINE: Oscillator config, Oscillator control, LFO rate, Filter cutoff, Filter resonance, Filter envelope amount, Amp attack, Amp release",
		"EFFECTS: FX amount, Delay mix, Delay feedback, Reverb mix"
	],
	"notice": "Keyboard version, distinct from the legacy Lead A1R module. Configure Global and Slot channels in the MIDI menu. Incoming wheel/pedal Morph uses CC11; CC1 is the transmitted modulation-wheel message and is not supplied here as an assumed incoming equivalent. Match the instrument MIDI channel and receive filters before sending notes or CCs. USB carries MIDI/data rather than audio; connect the audio outputs separately. Consult the download page for the correct Windows USB driver. Port aliases have not been verified on hardware; select the profile manually. The drawings are selected-control schematics rather than scale panel plans. Keyboard and panel controls remain unbound; splits, octave shifts and layer routing can change their behavior. Only the listed CCs are supplied, not the full MIDI implementation.",
